window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Death has come for us.<br> <br> With Ransom in Thanatos’s hands, the worst has happened. The god of death has everything he needs to break the shadow curse and loose the starving fangers on the innocents of Azar. <br> <br> I can’t let that happen. The serviles grow more restless, raiding the borders, and the vampire queen is powerless against them. Now, it’s a race against the clock to free Ransom and prevent an all-out war. Without my fated mate at my side, I can barely breathe, let alone lead the sicari.<br> <br> I have to find the strength, because there’s nothing I won’t do to get Ransom back. He promised me forever, and I’m holding him to it. Even if it means taking down the mother fangin’ god of death.</p> <p>***This is an upper YA/NA crossover with schmexy, sinful vampires, and is best suited for ages 17+. Be warned: this is a slow burn enemies-to-lovers romance, and the steaminess factor does increase through the course of the series! ♥</p> <p><i>***Vampish</i> is set within the world of Azar, along with (in listening order) <i>Hitched, Darkblood Academy, Royally Hitched, Darkblood Prison, </i>and <i>Wolfish,</i> but it's not necessary to listen to the other series first to enjoy this one.</p>"; 
